      en: "Ha Soai hydropower plant is located on the Malibamatso River in Lesotho's Butha-Buthe district. Commissioned in 2018, it generates 5 megawatts of electricity. The facility is part of the Lesotho Highlands Water Project, supplying water and power. It powers about 10,000 households. It harnesses the river's gradient for power generation. Construction cost $15 million. Ha Soai reduces reliance on imported electricity from South Africa and promotes renewable energy in Lesotho.",
